      {
        "id": 57018,
        "name": "flamethrower49",
        "username": "flamethrower49",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/838e76/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-29T06:02:10.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So... start with a hero easily capable of killing it first. &nbsp;Fanatic, Ra, Haka, Tempest, or Young Legacy for example. &nbsp;Especially Young Legacy.</p><p>That's not required, though. &nbsp;Remember that you don't HAVE to draw a card at the end of your turn. &nbsp;Your first couple heroes can skip their draw until you get to the heroes that can kill it. &nbsp;This stunts their development, sure, but it's usually better than the alternative. &nbsp;Needless to say, killing the Tome is Priority One, at all costs. &nbsp;Most teams should be able to field 3 damage between them round one, somehow. &nbsp;The worst are the games where he finds his Orb of Delirium or the Runes of Malediction (or both) to complement the Tome. &nbsp;Some of those might not be winnable.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:32:13.900Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
